    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;3.06</strong> Solitary plasmacytoma of bone: differential diagnosis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Judith A. Ferry",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 697.9pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 40.1pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.1pt;\" width=\"145\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Diagnosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.1pt;\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.1pt;\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Morphology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.1pt;\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunoglobulin (Ig) expressed</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.1pt;\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunophenotype, additional features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.1pt;\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cytogenetic/genetic features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"145\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Solitary plasmacytoma of bone</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Isolated lytic lesion of bone, often painful, +/&minus; fracture; no association with immunodeficiency</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffuse, destructive infiltrate of mature, immature, lymphocyte-like, plasmablast-like, or rarely anaplastic plasma cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monotypic cytoplasmic Ig light chain; IgG &gt; IgA &gt; light chain only; others rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">As for plasma cell myeloma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Similar to plasma cell myeloma, but not as extensively studied</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"145\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Chronic osteomyelitis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Fever, local pain</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mature plasma cells, +/&minus; lymphocytes, granulocytes, fibrosis, and necrotic bone</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Polytypic cytoplasmic Ig light chain</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD138+, CD38+, CD19+, CD56&minus; plasma cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No abnormalities</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"145\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Plasmablastic lymphoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Immunosuppressed patient with extranodal lesion (oral cavity, gastrointestinal, others; bone involvement is uncommon), usually without lymphadenopathy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffuse infiltrate of plasmablasts +/&minus; differentiation to more-mature plasma cells; high mitotic count; may have starry-sky appearance</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monotypic cytoplasmic Ig light chain +/&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD138+, CD38+, IRF4 (MUM1)+, MYC+, CD45+/&minus;, CD79a+/&minus;, CD56+/&minus;, CD20&minus;, PAX5&minus;, BCL6&minus;, ALK&minus;, HHV8&minus;, Ki-67 high; EBER usually positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Complex karyotype; <em>MYC</em> often rearranged, less often amplified</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"145\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Symptoms usually related to anaemia and paraprotein, +/&minus; autoimmune phenomena or cryoglobulinaemia; lymphadenopathy and/or splenomegaly may be present; discrete bone lesions are rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffuse, interstitial, or patchy involvement by small lymphocytes, plasma cells, and plasmacytoid lymphocytes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monotypic surface and cytoplasmic Ig light chain; IgM+, almost all cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD19+, CD20+, CD5&minus;, CD10&minus;, BCL6&minus;, CD23&minus;&nbsp;clonal B cells and clonal plasma cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>MYD88</em> p.Leu265Pro point mutation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"145\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Plasma cell myeloma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Most patients have symptoms related to CRAB, infections, and bleeding; some are asymptomatic and may have smouldering myeloma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffuse, interstitial, or patchy marrow involvement by mature, immature, lymphocyte-like, plasmablast-like, or rarely anaplastic plasma cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monotypic cytoplasmic Ig light chain; IgG &gt; IgA &gt; light chain only; others rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD138+, CD38+, IRF4 (MUM1)+, CD45&minus; or dim, CD19&minus;, CD56+; cyclin&nbsp;D1+ (in cases with <em>CCND1</em> rearrangement); minority: CD20+, KIT (CD117)+, CD10+; Ki-67 usually low; EBER almost always negative</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 117.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"157\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Hyperdiploid cases (~45%):</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">48&ndash;75&nbsp;chromosomes; gains of &ge;&nbsp;3&nbsp;of odd-numbered chromosomes: 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 15, 19, 21</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Non-hyperdiploid cases (~50%):</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Translocation of IGH with <em>CCND1</em> (most common), <em>MAF</em>, or <em>FGFR3</em>/<em>NSD2 </em>(<em>FGFR3</em>/<em>MMSET</em>); rare IGH partners (&le;&nbsp;2% of cases): <em>CCND3</em>, <em>CCND2</em>, <em>MAFA</em>, or <em>MAFB</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Other changes:</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Activating mutations of <em>KRAS</em>, <em>NRAS</em>, or <em>BRAF</em>; mutations activating NF-&kappa;B; <em>MYC</em> translocation; <em>TP53</em> abnormalities</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CRAB, hypercalcaemia, renal insufficiency, anaemia, and bone lesions. EBER, EBV-encoded small RNA.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]